# YOLO Tourney and OCR Bot Changelog

## Release 2.5.0 — Path 2 reliability hardening (2026-10-24)

- Added whole-image, single-consumer OCR queuing with a bounded backlog; attachment downloads now occur inside the queue so queued screenshots do not allocate unbounded in-memory image buffers.
- Hardened timeout recovery: after cleanup, the queue verifies the timed-out task settles; if it remains active—or cleanup itself stalls—OCR fails closed and tells the operator to restart instead of permitting overlapping work.
- Preserved pending correction state if an attachment is unsupported or the OCR queue is full; a replacement correction is cleared only when the queued screenshot actually starts processing.
- Added independent per-player/event score comparisons for a randomized 50-player dataset using formula functions extracted from the workbook HTML, including non-default multipliers, tier powers, and Grand Yolo weights.
- Added SQLite WAL checkpointing on clean store shutdown and a physical closed-database copy/reopen/integrity regression alongside JSON archive recovery tests.
- Updated the OCR regression report provenance to identify the selected engine honestly and record fixture runs/build metadata.
- Release validation remains conditional: the current host uses Node.js 22.16.0 and test-only dependency shims; clean `npm ci` on Node.js 24.17+, real-package Tesseract.js fallback, and real Discord login/permissions still require target-environment verification.


